                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature attempts to leave area <strong>F3</strong> while carrying anything edible, even a consumable such as an elixir or potion</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> An icy draft rises from the runes and whirls about the triggering creature. The creature takes @Damage[(6d12+35)[cold]] damage, with a @Check[fortitude|dc:37|basic|options:inflicts:slowed] save. On a failure, the creature is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Slowed]{Slowed 1} for 1 minute. On critical failure, the creature is instead @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Petrified] as they become encased in a layer of ice. A creature petrified in this way can be restored if exposed to a significant heat source (such as a campfire) for 10 minutes.</p>"
